{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Point"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(json:warnings:)","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(start:end:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/jsonObject"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONObjectEncodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueDecodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueEncodable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" boundary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" boundary point.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"window.selection"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that designates a child text node."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary points."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/domrange"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"This construct enables a serializable representation of a DOM Range.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared8DOMRangeV","title":"DOMRange","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}],"navigat